# Petri persona audit — Open Character Training arms on gemma-3-4b-it
#
# Copy to .env at this directory (the repo root) and fill in what you need:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The repo root is the right place for it. run_flourishing.py calls
# dotenv.load_dotenv(override=True), which walks up from
# petri/persona_audits/, so a .env here is found whether you run from the
# root or from petri/. Root .gitignore already ignores .env — never commit it.
#
# surf/scripts/serve_targets.sh is the exception: it sources surf/.env by
# path and does not walk up. Point it at this one file rather than keeping
# two copies in sync:
#
#   ln -s ../.env surf/.env
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. SERVING THE TARGET ARMS  (needed by surf/scripts/serve_targets.sh)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# google/gemma-3-4b-it is a GATED repo (gated: manual), and vLLM downloads the
# base itself at serve time. Two steps, both required:
#
#   1. accept the licence at https://huggingface.co/google/gemma-3-4b-it
#      with the same account the token belongs to
#   2. put a read-scope token here
#
# Without this, the server dies minutes into startup. Check it in seconds
# instead, before serving anything:
#
#   cd surf && .venv/bin/python -I scripts/fetch_persona_adapters.py
#
# The adapters themselves (maius/gemma-3-4b-it-personas) are public and are
# already downloaded to adapters/ — this token is only for the base.
HF_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. REACHING THE SERVED ARMS  (needed by the audit)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# inspect's vllm provider talks to an already-running server when
# VLLM_BASE_URL is set; without it, it tries to start its own, which cannot
# load LoRA subfolders. Leave these as they are unless you move the port.
#
# Target strings, once serve_targets.sh is up (bare adapter names are treated
# as preloaded on the external server, so nothing is re-downloaded):
#
#   base         vllm/google/gemma-3-4b-it
#   goodness     vllm/google/gemma-3-4b-it:goodness
#   sycophancy   vllm/google/gemma-3-4b-it:sycophancy
#
VLLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/v1

# The server is started without --api-key, so it accepts anything. inspect
# defaults this to "inspectai" if unset; set it explicitly so the value in
# the logs is not a surprise.
VLLM_API_KEY=dummy

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. AUDITOR AND JUDGE  (needed by the audit; this is the whole API spend)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DeepInfra, reached through inspect's OpenAI-compatible provider. The model
# string is openai-api/<service>/<model>, and the service prefix picks the env
# vars: "deepinfra" -> DEEPINFRA_API_KEY + DEEPINFRA_BASE_URL. Only the FIRST
# path segment is stripped as the service, so a model id that itself contains a
# slash works unchanged:
#
#   --auditor openai-api/deepinfra/anthropic/claude-opus-5-5
#   --judge   openai-api/deepinfra/anthropic/claude-opus-5-5
#
# NOTE ON THE RECORDED DEFAULT. run_flourishing.py still defaults both roles to
# openrouter/anthropic/claude-opus-4.5. DeepInfra does not serve opus-4.5 at
# all, so on this account you MUST pass --auditor and --judge explicitly. What
# DeepInfra does serve from Anthropic, checked 2026-11-15:
#
#   claude-opus-5-5  claude-opus-5  claude-opus-4-8  claude-opus-4-7
#   claude-sonnet-5-5  claude-sonnet-5  claude-sonnet-4-6
#   claude-haiku-4-5  claude-fable-5
#
# Any of these is a deviation from the recorded default, so record which one a
# run used. opus-4-7/4-8 are the closest to it; opus-5-5 is a generation newer
# and more capable but not comparable with the repo's existing audits.
#
# Tool calling over this route was verified for opus-5-5 and sonnet-5-5 — the
# auditor needs it for send_message, so it is not optional.
DEEPINFRA_API_KEY=
DEEPINFRA_BASE_URL=https://api.deepinfra.com/v1/openai

# Only if you route the auditor/judge straight to Anthropic instead
# (--auditor/--judge anthropic/...). Leave empty when using DeepInfra.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
